Category: IT Services

Location: Fort Western Province Sri Lanka

For an international organization in Europe, we are urgently looking for a REMOTE Senior Java developer - Angular / NodeJS with good knowledge of Angular (Angular, AngularJS, Angular2, …). The Senior Java developer - Angular / NodeJS is responsible for the design, implementation, testing, deployment, and support of multiple applications.

Candidates need to be able to work the European schedule.

During the corona crisis, interviews will be done through WEBEX, and travel is not required for the interviews. All positions are long-term.

Tasks and Responsibilities:

• Ensure the project's technical knowledge is kept within the contracted company for the duration of the services;

• Perform the initial transfer of knowledge;

• Onsite or near-shore development, testing, and delivery of the Work Package in the development and maintenance environments, as well as assistance to migration to production if requested, as further detailed below under "deliverables".Troubleshoot and remediate system problems affecting availability and functionality;

• Generate and retain relevant technical documentation related to the technical services provided during the project period;

• Resolution of minor open issues relating to the 2017 IT enhancement project, depending on time availability and re-evaluation of project priorities if necessary;

• Troubleshooting and remediation of system issues impacting the availability or functionality of the systems, including its internal administrative interface, database, website, and the related supporting functions to internal and external collaborators;

Experience:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +5 years of experience working with software development skills (Java, Angular.js, Spring, or JPA) and knowledge of service-oriented architecture;

• Excellent knowledge of internet technologies including Angular.js, Rest APIs, Jquery, JavaScript, NodeJs, JAVA and SQL or UI design, CSS, HTML, and related technologies;

• Good knowledge of software development practices (version control systems: SVN, GIT, etc.), and deployment methodologies (Docker, development/acceptance/production);

• Knowledge of data analysis and modeling, in particular with database systems including MySQL or similar products;

• Fluent in English;

Desirable:

• Experience with Unix operating system (bash, ant, docker, RSA, svn). Experience with service-oriented architecture;

• Experience with AWS and the following resources: Cloudformation Templates, EC2 Amazon Linux, S3, Lambda, ECS, RDS, ALB, and Cloud Front;

• Experience in Search Engine Optimization;

• Good knowledge of search engines (with a preference to Lucene-based search engines: Elasticsearch technology and/or Solr);

• Good knowledge of XML parsing and transformation;

Offered:

• A challenging role for an international organization;

• Attractive salary package or freelance rate;

Interested :

Please send your resume and motivation to or call us on +94 114312515 for more information.

